# Ignore list for the ROOT of the runtime copy of the pinned evidence tree.
#
# run_real_query.py writes this file to `.aftignore` at the top of the copied
# tree, beside the copy of this directory's own .aftignore. It is needed
# because an .aftignore only applies below its own directory, the way a
# .gitignore does, so the list in benchmarks/aft-search/ cannot reach files
# elsewhere in the tree.
#
# The pinned tree carries a report under .alfonso/ that quotes the concept
# fixtures' queries. Indexed, it becomes a self-fulfilling exact hit for those
# queries, the same answer-key problem this directory's .aftignore solves for
# the fixture files. The repository's .gitignore would normally hide it, but
# the copy has no .git directory, so AFT does not apply .gitignore there.
#
# The last entry keeps this file itself out of the index, so the only change
# to the candidate pool is the removal of the report.
/.alfonso/reports/search-fusion-quality.md
/.aftignore
